                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S^V, S^V)
              is a matching pair of
              = succeed "-spaces" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#RepresentationSphereToRepresentationSphereIsMatchingPair"}
            %p
              This equivariant Hopf degree theorem is stated above under the simplifying assumption that the dimension of all fixed loci is positive. But the proof from
              %a{:href => "#tomDieck79"} tomDieck 79, 8.4
              immediately applies to our situation where the dimension of the fixed locus at the full subgroup
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H = G
              may be 0, with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mrow
